        <fma:definition>A graft is a segment of healthy tissue transplanted from one area of a person&apos;s body to another. Unlike a flap, a graft initially relies solely on diffusion for nourishment, and its blood supply is later established through neovascularization—primarily via newly formed capillary networks—which develops a significant time after transplantation.</fma:definition>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Surgical graft</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


